task: wasm-playground-vtables::flat_hir_codec
status: done
desc: Serialize and reconstruct module-local HIR vtable rows in flat-HIR version 7.
impl:
  - First add a public encode/decode round-trip test for two vtables and dynamic expression references.
  - Assert version 6 blobs are rejected after the format version changes to 7.
  - Add vtable section marker 6 after safety proofs, with bounded counts and ordered function slots.
  - Keep the exported WASM ABI version at 2.
tests:
  | id | dado | quando | então |
  | H-1 | HIR with two vtables and dyn references | encode then decode | names, ordered slots, and expression references survive |
  | H-2 | flat-HIR blob with version word 6 | decode version-7 format | decoder rejects it as an invalid header |

[3]
task: wasm-playground-vtables::wasm_dyn_execution
status: done
desc: Complete the flat-HIR type metadata required by dynamic dispatch and verify both public WASM execution paths.
impl:
  - Preserve struct definitions, ordered fields, field types, and layout metadata in flat-HIR version 7.
  - Add a public round-trip assertion that decoded concrete struct definitions preserve field reads.
  - Reuse the two-implementation Biased fixture whose native VM result is 73.
  - Exercise zith_emit_hir plus zith_execute_hir and the direct zith_run_source path.
  - Build the WASM artifact in /tmp and run the existing Node runtime harness against it.
  - Keep the existing native test_dyn_method_dispatch regression unchanged.
tests:
  | id | dado | quando | então |
  | W-0 | First and Second struct definitions | encode then decode | names and ordered field layouts survive |
  | W-1 | Biased fixture through encoded HIR | execute decoded HIR | ABI status is 0 and guest exit code is 73 |
  | W-2 | Biased fixture through run_source | compile and execute source | ABI status is 0 and guest exit code is 73 |

[4]
task: wasm-playground-vtables::browser_command_chain
status: done
desc: Add limited sequential && chaining to the browser terminal only.
impl:
  - Add a DOM-free browser/CommonJS helper for parsing and dispatching command chains.
  - Validate the entire chain and reject empty segments before dispatching any command.
  - Dispatch left to right and stop on false; do not add general shell parsing.
  - Preserve clear behavior and make run return failure for nonzero guest exits.
  - Echo the original command once, document chaining in help, and load the helper first.
tests:
  | id | dado | quando | então |
  | C-1 | clear && run | browser terminal dispatches chain | old output clears and the current editor buffer runs |
  | C-2 | whitespace around nonempty commands | parse chain | segments are trimmed and preserve order |
  | C-3 | empty leading, middle, or trailing segment | parse then dispatch | chain is rejected before any command executes |
  | C-4 | command dispatcher returns false | run a multi-command chain | later commands are skipped |

